  "worked_solution": "To compute\n\n$$\na\u00f7b=\\frac{3(z-2)}{(z+1)^{2}}\u00f7\\frac{z-2}{6(z+1)},\n$$\n\nwe just need to multiply by the reciprocal of the divisor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3(z-2)}{(z+1)^{2}}\u00f7\\frac{z-2}{6(z+1)} & = \\\\ \\frac{3(z-2)}{(z+1)^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{6(z+1)}{z-2} & = \\\\ \\frac{3\\cancel{(z-2)}}{(z+1)^{\\cancel{2}}}\\cdot \\frac{6\\cancel{(z+1)}}{\\cancel{(z-2)}} & = \\\\ \\frac{3}{z+1}\\cdot 6 & = \\\\ \\frac{18}{z+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
